        "text": "Diagnosis:\n- Duplicate job executions were occurring because two scheduler instances (scheduler-a and scheduler-b) both believed they were leaders, causing jobs to be dispatched twice.\n- Logs confirmed a split-brain scenario: both schedulers held leadership due to a failed leader step-down.\n- Metrics showed two scheduler leaders for the past hour, instead of the expected single leader.\n\nRemediation:\n- I restarted the scheduler service to force a new, correct leader election.\n- After the restart, metrics confirmed only one leader remained, and duplicate job executions dropped to zero.\n- I posted a public status update indicating the incident is resolved and no further duplicate reports are being generated.\n\nThe issue is now resolved.",
